<title>USA: Mark Twain Bancshares sets higher payout.</title>
<headline>Mark Twain Bancshares sets higher payout.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarterly</p>
<p>			  Latest		     Prior</p>
<p> Amount		 $ 0.41		     $0.35</p>
<p> Pay		     May 9</p>
<p> Record	     April 18</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name is Mark Twain Bancshares Inc.</p>
<p>The increased dividend rate is in accordance with the merger agreement between Mark Twain Bancshares and Mercantile Bancorp Inc Inc, which allows a dividend to be declared and paid by Mark Twain equivalent to 0.952 times the current quarterly dividend rate paid on Mercantile common. The pending merger with Mercantile is subject to shareholder approval and is expected to occur April 25, 1997.</p>
<p>		((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
